{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507259-what-would-you-do-if-your-group-of-pcs-decided-to-help-voormas","id":1507259,"title":"What would you do if your group of PCs decided to help Voormas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-02T21:19:11-07:00","id":1507259,"title":"What would you do if your group of PCs decided to help Voormas?","content":"Ok, so let's discuss something very rare in RPGs that is a scenario where the villain actually win in the end, but this case is even rarer because the players' characters actually want to help the Antagonist reach his goals. How would you as a storyteller deal with this situation? Lastly, but far from less important is how can you make a scenario where the villain win fun for the group?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T10:10:33-07:00","id":1508049,"title":"","content":"It's simple. The PC's would now have to face enemies who do oppose voormas. He himself can not be everywhere at once.<br /> It's funny because the nephandi and the like would still be their enemies. The usual good guys such as senex or Dante might be presented as dangerous ideologues who, from pov of the characters, do not care if the world burns for the sake of risking everything for a coin toss. <br /> <br /> <br /> Remember that he is not evil for evils sake. Or rather he is evil but his specific goal is not. I would present such a victory as bitter-sweet. After all, complete Armageddon has just been prevented, albeit at the cost of a static half dead universe. Death has been beaten. Here, both villainous and heroic PC's might like or tolerate the outcome albeit for different reasons <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> So, yeah, I think a storyteller should be prepared for all scenarios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T12:53:51-07:00","id":1508063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507259-what-would-you-do-if-your-group-of-pcs-decided-to-help-voormas?p=1508049#post1508049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's simple. The PC's would now have to face enemies who do oppose voormas. He himself can not be everywhere at once.<br /> It's funny because the nephandi and the like would still be their enemies. The usual good guys such as senex or Dante might be presented as dangerous ideologues who, from pov of the characters, do not care if the world burns for the sake of risking everything for a coin toss.<br /> <br /> <br /> Remember that he is not evil for evils sake. Or rather he is evil but his specific goal is not. I would present such a victory as bitter-sweet. After all, complete Armageddon has just been prevented, albeit at the cost of a static half dead universe. Death has been beaten. Here, both villainous and heroic PC's might like or tolerate the outcome albeit for different reasons<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> So, yeah, I think a storyteller should be prepared for all scenarios.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if a game in such scenario would be possible or at least enjoyable/interesting. One thing the books don't explore is how such a world would work. It would be interesting, because otherwise we get the impression that Voormas' defeat predetermined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T19:09:37-07:00","id":1508106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507259-what-would-you-do-if-your-group-of-pcs-decided-to-help-voormas?p=1508063#post1508063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder if a game in such scenario would be possible or at least enjoyable/interesting. One thing the books don't explore is how such a world would work. It would be interesting, because otherwise we get the impression that Voormas' defeat predetermined.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does say that &quot;awakening would be impossible&quot; does it not? Should Voormas win. Though it also says that true death would not exist, a narcosynthesis of, i assume, the underworld and the material. I admit that's a bit daunting to portray","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T00:09:47-07:00","id":1508122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1507259-what-would-you-do-if-your-group-of-pcs-decided-to-help-voormas?p=1508106#post1508106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does say that &quot;awakening would be impossible&quot; does it not? Should Voormas win. Though it also says that true death would not exist, a narcosynthesis of, i assume, the underworld and the material. I admit that's a bit daunting to portray</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I see that it's too &quot;otherworldy&quot; to portray, but I'm always curious to know if someone has ever gone this way. Like portraying one of the Gehenna scenarios, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister